# NightForge project rules

## Branches

- `production/langgraph` is the only branch to commit to. Work happens here.
- `main` is the public portfolio snapshot. Never commit to it directly.
- `archive/crewai-prototype` is frozen. Do not push to it.
- If a task forces an `agent/*` or `cursor/*` branch, open the PR into `production/langgraph`.
- Never touch the `DannyBarren/nightforge` repository from this one.

See [docs/PRODUCTION.md](../../docs/PRODUCTION.md) for what each branch holds.

## Package layout

- `leadforge/` is the CrewAI + Streamlit prototype. Keep it working. Do not delete
  `leadforge/`, `app.py`, or the CrewAI pipeline, and do not refactor them to serve the
  new code.
- `nightforge/` is the new production package: LangGraph graphs plus a FastAPI surface.
  It lives beside the prototype, not on top of it.
- Reuse the Pydantic contracts in `leadforge/models.py` — `DiscoveredLead`,
  `LeadResearch`, `PitchOutput`, `RunManifest`. Do not fork parallel model definitions.
- Port `leadforge/cost_tracker.py` and `leadforge/guardrails.py` into the new package.
  They are the reason this thing is safe to run overnight; they do not get thrown away
  and rewritten from scratch.

## No send path

- There is no email or SMS send path anywhere in this repo, and none gets added.
- `Human Review` on every research export row is always `YES`.
  `PitchOutput.human_review_required` stays `True` after validation, including when an
  LLM tries to set it false.

## Governor

- A budget/guardrail check runs **before** every LLM call and every paid search call.
  Pre-call gate, not post-call accounting.
- Fail closed. If the governor cannot confirm budget, the call does not happen.
- A budget stop is a clean stop: mark the run `stopped_early` with a `stop_reason`,
  export what completed, do not crash.
- Hard ceiling stays $10, recommended cap $8, projected early stop $7.25.

## Adapters

- Vendor APIs live behind adapters. Graph and node code never imports a Jobber,
  Housecall Pro, or other vendor SDK directly — it talks to the adapter interface.
- Do not invent or hardcode Jobber OAuth credentials. The adapter is a stub until real
  credentials exist outside this repo.

## Fail closed

Budget, webhook signature verification, and auth all fail closed. Missing config,
an unverifiable signature, or an unresolved identity means reject — never a default-allow
or a silent pass-through.

## Data and content

- Public web data only. No scraping behind a login wall, no private databases.
- Sample mode must still produce 3 complete rows when search or the LLM flakes. The
  seed top-up and deterministic fallback pitch exist for that and stay that way.
- Demo data stays obviously fake: `example.com` addresses, 555 phone numbers, labeled
  as demo seeds.
- This repo is public. No pricing, no DPA text, no commercial strategy, no client names.

## Working style

- Keep changes scoped to what was asked. Stop when the checklist is done.
- Run the tests you touch (`make test` / `pytest -q`).
